diff --git a/docs/metrics.md b/docs/metrics.md
index 29cd3ab..d2171cd 100644
--- a/docs/metrics.md
+++ b/docs/metrics.md
@@ -35,6 +35,23 @@ Once the exporter `Deployment` is ready, `mariadb-operator` creates a [ServiceMo
 
 As you scale your MariaDB with more or less replicas, `mariadb-operator` will reconcile the `ServiceMonitor` to add/remove targets related to the MariaDB instances. 
 
+If you don't need the `ServiceMonitor`, for instance because Prometheus is running outside of the cluster and the `ServiceMonitor` CRD is not installed, you can disable it by setting `spec.metrics.serviceMonitor.enabled = false`. The exporter `Deployment` and `Service` will still be created, so they can be scraped by other means:
+
+```yaml
+apiVersion: k8s.mariadb.com/v1alpha1
+kind: MariaDB
+metadata:
+  name: mariadb
+spec:
+...
+  metrics:
+    enabled: true
+    serviceMonitor:
+      enabled: false
+```
+
+The same `spec.metrics.serviceMonitor.enabled` field is available in the `MaxScale` resource.
+
 ## Configuration
 
 The easiest way to setup metrics in your MariaDB instance is just by setting `spec.metrics.enabled = true`, like in this [example](../examples/manifests/mariadb_metrics.yaml):
diff --git a/internal/controller/mariadb_controller_metrics.go b/internal/controller/mariadb_controller_metrics.go
